/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/ Fully lazy end-to-end pipeline.
/
/ Reads two parquet files, joins them, derives columns, aggregates, sorts, and
/ streams the result straight to another parquet file. Nothing is ever
/ materialised into an in-memory table — every binding stays a lazy plan and the
/ only execution happens when `>>` sinks the final plan to disk.
/
/ Run from the repo root:
/   cargo run -- examples/lazy_join_pipeline.qpl
/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/ 1. scan both inputs as lazy plans (no IO yet)
trades: lazy load `examples/data/trades.parquet
quotes: lazy load `examples/data/quotes.parquet

/ 2. left-join quotes onto trades by sym (still lazy — the join is just plan nodes)
enriched: select sym, side, price, size, bid, ask from trades `sym lj quotes `sym

/ 3. derive spread + notional, keep the frame lazy by re-assigning the binding
enriched: update spread: ask - bid, notional: price * size from enriched

/ 4. tag each row as a wide or tight market
enriched: update band: ?[spread > 0.4; `wide; `tight] from enriched

/ 5. aggregate per sym/side/band, then sort — all lazy
summary: select traded: sum notional, avg_spread: avg spread, n: count price by sym, side, band from enriched
summary: `traded`sym!10b `summary

/ show the plan
`summary

o: "examples/data/market_summary.parquet"
/ 6. the ONLY execution: stream the final plan to parquet without collecting
`summary >> `$o

log "created parquet file: '" o "'"
